---
// <BcnDraftKind> — the styles for a draft's kind mark, built at run time by draftKind() in
// ./draft-kind.ts. Render this once on a page that shows draft rows.
//
// An obligation is develop's obligation-class-chip, 11px at weight 500 on a 14% tint of its
// class hue, the text at 78% of the hue toward black. Adhere reads --color-obligation,
// Monitor and Notify their own hues, Roster --color-action. An action is its requirement
// type on the same chip in --color-action, cut to its column when long.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: esa-badge's variants are status tones, not a hue per obligation class,
// and it has no hook for a class hue. Checked Beacon: obligation-class-chip and the
// the type chip is its metrics in the action color. bcn-draft-kind is its home.
---

<style is:global>
  .bcn-draft-kind { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .bcn-draft-kind--class {
    --_hue: var(--color-obligation);
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 1px var(--spacing-200);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 4px);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.5;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--_hue) 14%, var(--color-background-elevation-raised));
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--_hue) 78%, var(--color-content-default));
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .bcn-draft-kind--class[data-class='monitor'] { --_hue: var(--color-obligation-monitor); }
  .bcn-draft-kind--class[data-class='notify'] { --_hue: var(--color-obligation-notify); }
  .bcn-draft-kind--class:is([data-class='roster'], [data-class='action']) { --_hue: var(--color-action); }
</style>
